  "id": "20_Leaders_Who_Built_the_CISO_Era_2_Decades_of_Change_txt_155",
  "content": "Make no mistake, Joe Sullivan, Uber's former chief security officer (CSO), is a controversial figure. In 2022, a jury convicted him of covering up a breach against Uber that occurred in 2016. Not only did Sullivan not publicly disclose the breach — the theft of data belonging to 57 million Uber riders and drivers — when it happened, he hid key details from the Federal Trade Commission (FTC). Even after pressed, he didn't disclose the fact that Uber, under his recommendation, paid off the cyberattackers behind the breach and had them sign a nondisclosure agreement.",
